    historyContent: {
      origins: "First appearing in the early 1500s. Its name means 'First' and refers to the primacy of the 'Primiera' hand. It was a favorite of monarchs, including Henry VIII and Catherine de' Medici.",
      originCountries: [
        'Italy',
      ],
      timeline: [
        '1526: First legal mention in Italian gambling records.',
        '1550s: Becomes the most popular gambling game in London and Venice.',
        "1700s: Gradually evolves into the French game 'Ambigu' and then into 'Poque'.",
        "Present: Survival as a scoring component in the game 'Scopa', but rarely played as a standalone game.",
      ],
      evolution: "Primiera introduced the concept of 'Vying' (the bet/raise/fold mechanic) which is the defining characteristic of the Poker lineage.",
      cultural: 'Commonly depicted in Renaissance literature as a metaphor for the unpredictability of fate and the power of deception (bluffing).',
    },
